cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "diffcohesive: a differentiable cohesive-zone fracture solver"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/roysondsouza316/diffcohesive"
authors:
  # TODO: confirm affiliation/ORCID before release:
  - family-names: "Dsouza"
    given-names: "Royson"
    affiliation: "VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland"
abstract: >
  A GPU-accelerated, end-to-end differentiable cohesive-zone fracture solver
  built on the TensorMesh PyTorch-native finite element library. The entire
  forward solve (Newton path-following with a handoff to Crisfield/Riks
  arc-length through softening) is differentiable via implicit
  differentiation/adjoint, enabling gradient-based identification of
  analytic (bilinear Camanho-Davila/Turon, Benzeggagh-Kenane mixed-mode) or
  neural-network-based traction-separation laws from load-displacement data, in place of
  the derivative-free genetic-algorithm calibration that otherwise dominates
  the cohesive-zone-model identification literature.
keywords:
  - cohesive zone model
  - fracture mechanics
  - delamination
  - differentiable simulation
  - finite element method
  - automatic differentiation
  - implicit differentiation
  - inverse identification
